# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "An ni: name stops at a quote, a backtick or a closing angle"

# The ni: body took any run without `;` or whitespace, so an ni: lacking its own `;` reached forward to a
# later one, swallowing the value's closing backtick and the call's `>>`; the call never closed.

<<~ x a=`ni:///x`>>;abc tail
#                ^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5

after the call
#^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5
#^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - meta.attribute.widget.html.tiddlywiki5

<<~ x a="ni:///x">>;abc tail
#                ^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5

after the call
#^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5
#^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - meta.attribute.widget.html.tiddlywiki5

# CONTROL: a whole ni: name still reads its algorithm and digest.

<<^ code=`&#x0003;` bcc=`ni:///sha-256;7uFf47o8VMhpXmwKCHt2Ev8Kyin9lwMX-N3DlYeX73k`>>
#                              ^^^^^^^ support.type.algorithm.ni.memetic-wikitext
#                                      ^^^^ constant.other.checksum.ni.memetic-wikitext

after the call
#^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5
#^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - meta.attribute.widget.html.tiddlywiki5
